---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii3_165",
  "series": "Band II 3 (1695 - 1700)",
  "seq": 165,
  "text": "<p> [[425.12]] <b>165. LEIBNIZ AN JOHANN CHRISTIAN SCHULENBURG</p>\n<p> [[425.13]] Hannover, 29. März (8. April) 1698. [155.168.]</b></p>\n\n<p> [[426.5]] Vir celeberrime </p>\n<p> [[426.6]] Etsi <Fn><i>Am Kopf der Seite von Leibniz' Hand</i>: Ad Dn. Schulenburgium rectorem Bremensem</Fn> Dominus Sanderus plus petierit meo nomine, quam ipse ego fuissem ausus, qui\n[[426.7]] tempore Tuo abuti nollem, plurimum tamen lucri inde ad me pervenit literis a Te acceptis\n[[426.8]] humanissimis, et muneribus etiam quibus plurimum sum delectatus et gratias debeo singulares.\n[[426.9]] Utraque dissertatio quam misisti argumenti mihi pergrati est. Nam urnae repertae sub tumulis,\n[[426.10]] de quibus Blumianae theses, antiquitates harum regionum illustrant. Calculi vero Mathematici\n[[426.11]] applicatio ad usum ac praeterea ^#.[ratiocinia <Fn><i>In E</i>: ratiocinia in Metaphysicis</Fn> a Metaphysicis^#.] semimathematica, quae utraque in\n[[426.12]] Knolleanis reperi, plane sunt ad palatum meum. Velim delineatas haberi urnas, caeteraque\n[[426.13]] ^#.[quae <Fn><i>In E</i>: quae praefatione</Fn> in praefatione^#.] memoras; et Dn. Knolleum pergere optem in his quae ornare coepit,\n[[426.14]] studiis illustrandis. Ejus Meditatio Metaphysica habere mihi visa est aliquid pulchri et profundi,\n[[426.15]] et, si hoc quoque addere licet, congrui ad sensus meos. </p>\n<p> [[426.16]] Nimirum fines seu limites sunt de Essentia Creaturarum, limites autem sunt aliquid\n[[426.17]] privativum, consistuntque in negatione progressus ulterioris. Interim fatendum est, creaturam,\n[[426.18]] postquam jam valorem a Deo nacta est, qualisque in sensus incurrit, aliquid etiam positivum\n[[426.19]] continere, seu aliquid habere ultra fines neque adeo in meros limites seu indivisibilia posse\n[[426.20]] resolvi. Ac proinde etiam ex ipsiusmet Thesium autoris (puto) sententia, ^#.[<b>postulatum <Fn><i>In E</i>: <b>postulatum</b>; ex</Fn>\n[[426.21]] sejungendi</b>; ex^#.] quo resolutionem in meros fines, seu mera indivisibilia infert, ad creaturam\n[[426.22]] cum valore sumtam applicari non posse. </p>\n<p> [[427.1]] Atque hic valor, cum consistat in positivo, est quidam Perfectionis creatae gradus, cui\n[[427.2]] etiam agendi vis inest, quae, ut ego arbitror substantiae naturam constituit. Adeo ut valor ille a\n[[427.3]] Deo tributus, revera sit vigor, seu vis indita rebus, quam quidam frustra negant, non animadvertentes\n[[427.4]] sese ita praeter opinionem incidere in doctrinam Spinosae, qui Deum solum facit\n[[427.5]] substantiam, caetera ejus modos. </p>\n<p> [[427.6]] Atque haec est origo rerum ex Deo et nihilo, positivo et privativo, perfectione et imperfectione,\n[[427.7]] valore et limitibus, activo et passivo, forma (id est entelechia, nisu, vigore) et materia\n[[427.8]] seu mole, per se torpente nisi quod resistentiam habet. </p>\n<p> [[427.9]] Illustravi ista nonnihil origine numerorum ex 0 et 1 a me observata, quae pulcherrimum\n[[427.10]] est emblema perpetuae rerum creationis ex nihilo, ^#.[dependentiaeque <Fn><i>In E</i>: dependentiae, quae a</Fn> a^#.] Deo. Nam adhibita\n[[427.11]] progressione simplicissima nempe dyadica, loco decadicae vel quaternariae, omnes numeri\n[[427.12]] exprimi possunt per 0 et 1, ut in Tabula adjecta patet; in qua genesi\n[[427.13]] Numerorum quae maxime naturae convenit, multa latent mira ad meditationem,\n[[427.14]] imo et ad praxin, etsi non pro usu vulgari. </p>\n<p> [[427.15]] Caeterum rogo ut Dn. Knolleum data occasione, etiam meo (si tanti\n[[427.16]] videtur) nomine, horteris uti in praeclaris istis meditationibus pergat, qualium\n[[427.17]] similes saepe ab ipso videre velim sive in Mathematicis, sive in\n[[427.18]] philosophia illa altiore. Excitandum etiam putem ad colendam illam sublimiorem\n[[427.19]] Mathesin, quae continet Scientiam infiniti, cujus elementa quaedam\n[[427.20]] a me sunt prodita novo calculi genere proposito, quem Hugenius aliique praestantes viri\n[[427.21]] non sine plausu excepere, et quem nunc illustrarunt inprimis Domini Bernoullii fratres, et\n[[427.22]] peculiari ^#.[etiam <Fn><i>In E</i>: etiam dissertatione Dominus Marchio</Fn> libro Dn. Marchio^#.] Hospitalius Gallus. Et compertum est non alia melius\n[[427.23]] ^#.[ratione <Fn><i>in E</i>: ratione aperiri aditum a</Fn> transitum aperiri a^#.] Geometria ad naturam, quae per infinitos gradus intermedios in\n[[427.24]] omni mutatione (ut ego arbitror) progrediens, characterem habet autoris infiniti. </p>\n<p> [[428.1]] Quae olim mihi de nostro Solis incolatu ex praeclari Astronomi Dn. Eimarti placitis\n[[428.2]] indicari curaveras, verissima arbitror, si intelligamus tellurem esse inter planetas seu satellites\n[[428.3]] solis; sin altius aliquid subest, fatebor mentem autoris mihi non esse perspectam. Newtonus\n[[428.4]] Mathematicus excellens, Astrorum vortices tollendos putat; sed mihi ut olim in <i>Actis</i> Lipsiensium\n[[428.5]] prodidi non tantum conservari posse sed etiam pulcherrime procedere videntur, Circulatione\n[[428.6]] harmonica cujus admirandas deprehendi proprietates. </p>\n<p> [[428.7]] De observatis Eimartianis vellem aliquando nosse distinctiora, ac Tuis etiam doctissimis\n[[428.8]] cogitationibus frui. Sed agnosco occupationes Tuas laboriosas, et Valetudini etiam parum\n[[428.9]] firmae indoleo; meliora precatus, speransque; modo in tempore Tibi prospicias, quod faciendum\n[[428.10]] suadeo. Vale. Dabam Hanoverae 29. Martii 1698. </p>\n<p> [[428.11]] deditissimus ^#.[Godefridus^#.] <Fn><i>In E</i>: Godofredus</Fn> Guilielmus Leibnitius </p>\n",
  "number": "165.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN JOHANN CHRISTIAN SCHULENBURG",
  "date": "Hannover, 29. März (8. April) 1698. [155.168.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:165. LEIBNIZ AN JOHANN CHRISTIAN SCHULENBURG Hannover, 29. März (8. April) 1698. [155.168.] Vir celeberrime Etsi Am Kopf der Seite von Leibniz' Hand: Ad Dn. Schulenburgium rectorem Bremensem Dominus Sanderus plus petierit meo nomine, quam ipse ego fuissem ausus, qui tempore Tuo abuti nollem, plurimu...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>